; The structural half of the unikernel claim: link every offline package and no
; transport. If the closure acquires unix, lwt or a socket anywhere -- including
; inside a package we do not own -- this stops building, and test/no_io_guard.sh
; runs it.
;
; It is an ordinary executable rather than a Mirage build on purpose: the point
; is the dependency closure, and checking that needs no Solo5 toolchain. The
; other half -- a guest that actually boots -- is validation/solo5-image/, which
; does. See docs/unikernel.md.
;
; The offline packages are named individually because dune-project sets
; implicit_transitive_deps to false; naming them is also what makes this a
; check that each one links rather than only the umbrella.

(executable
 (name unikernel)
 (libraries
  cosmos
  cosmos-types
  cosmos-crypto
  cosmos-proto
  cosmos-tx
  cosmos-signer
  cosmos-rpc))
